# Waveshare ESP32-S3-Touch-LCD-4.3 Port Implementation Plan

> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (recommended) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan task-by-task. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.

**Goal:** Add a seventh board port — an 800×480 RGB parallel panel with GT911 touch, a CH422G IO expander, and no physical buttons — without introducing any `#ifdef BOARD_*` into shared code.

**Architecture:** A new `firmware/src/boards/waveshare_lcd_43/` folder implementing the existing HAL, plus a new PlatformIO env. Three pieces of pure logic (brightness dimming, the hot-corner hit test, usage-panel slot geometry) are extracted into dependency-free headers and unit-tested on the host, following the `src/splash_geometry.h` precedent. Everything hardware-dependent is verified by a bring-up ladder ordered riskiest-first.

**Tech Stack:** PlatformIO + pioarduino (Arduino Core 3.x), Arduino_GFX 1.6.4 (`Arduino_ESP32RGBPanel` + `Arduino_RGB_Display`), LVGL 9.2, NimBLE-Arduino 2.1.

**Spec:** `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-10-lcd-43-port-design.md`
**Branch:** `feat/lcd-43-port` (already created; the spec is committed there)

## Global Constraints

- **No `#ifdef BOARD_*` in shared code.** Shared files are `main.cpp`, `ui.cpp`, `splash.cpp`, and everything under `hal/`. Board differences go behind `BoardCaps` (runtime) or live in the board folder. See `docs/porting/capability-flags.md`.
- **No copyleft dependencies.** The CH422G and GT911 drivers are vendored as minimal readers, matching the existing FT3168/CST816T readers. Do not add `bb_captouch`, `Arduino_DriveBus`, or `ESP_IOExpander`.
- **Board env name:** `waveshare_lcd_43`. **Board folder:** `firmware/src/boards/waveshare_lcd_43/`. **Identity flag:** `-DBOARD_LCD_43`.
- **Arduino_GFX version floor:** `^1.6.4`. `bounce_buffer_size_px` and `getFrameBuffer()` require it.
- **Panel geometry:** 800×480, landscape, fixed orientation, no rotation.
- **Host unit tests** are plain C++17 with no Arduino/LVGL includes, built with `g++ -std=c++17 -I firmware/src`, using the `CHECK` macro pattern from `firmware/test/test_splash_geometry/test_main.cpp`.
- **Every task ends with a green build** of `pio run -d firmware -e waveshare_lcd_43`. Tasks touching `ui.cpp` additionally rebuild `waveshare_amoled_216` and `waveshare_lcd_154`.
- **Temporary instrumentation** (I2C scan, expander bit-walk, raw touch logging) is explicitly removed in Task 10. It must not survive into the final commit.

## Hardware reference (verified — do not re-derive)

| Signal | GPIO |
|---|---|
| DE / VSYNC / HSYNC / PCLK | 5 / 3 / 46 / 7 |
| R0–R4 | 1, 2, 42, 41, 40 |
| G0–G5 | 39, 0, 45, 48, 47, 21 |
| B0–B4 | 14, 38, 18, 17, 10 |
| I2C SDA / SCL | 8 / 9 |
| Touch INT | 4 |

Timing: hsync polarity 0, front 40, pulse 48, back 88; vsync polarity 0, front 13, pulse 3, back 32; `pclk_active_neg = 1`, 16 MHz.

CH422G (each I²C address *is* a register): `0x24` WR_SET (bit0 `IO_OE`), `0x38` WR_IO (outputs IO0–7, bit *n* = EXIO*n*), `0x23` WR_OC, `0x26` RD_IO. Power-on defaults: WR_SET `0x01` (IO0–7 already outputs), WR_IO `0xFF` (**all HIGH — the GT911 boots out of reset**). EXIO1 = touch reset, EXIO2 = backlight.

GT911: address 0x5D when INT is held low across reset release. Registers `0x8140` (product ID), `0x814E` (status), `0x8150` (point 1, 8 bytes: track id, x lo, x hi, y lo, y hi, size lo, size hi, reserved). Write 0 to `0x814E` after each read.

